950	{"artifactId":"TASK-64703b708590bd68-s1-t1","entry":{"id":"00mvy8pnug001-6a6880f1-ccf3-4cec-9ffd-de4eaf11dff3","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:45:46.744Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"The daemon's typecheck and the required unit test both passed, and independent inspection confirms the audit module, its test and the docs/plans document together satisfy all three acceptance checks: complete coverage of the real handler-runtime.ts methods and step phases (verified by independent extraction, not just trusting the implementer), correct repo/path param annotation on every modifying entry, and a written, importable scope decision for the daemon-store writers. Only the three task-scoped files (repo-call-audit.ts, its test, and the doc) were added; no other source was touched.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
821	{"artifactId":"TASK-64703b708590bd68-s1-t2","entry":{"id":"00mvy8sww8002-9a8c86e2-dd47-452c-adf6-df074d870866","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:48:18.440Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"src/daemon/repo-call-gate.ts implements FILE_MODIFYING_METHODS/RepoCallRule/RepoCallCheck/requireRepoForCall/gateRepoCall exactly as specified (five refusal codes, path rewriting against the named repo, symlink containment via realpath, run-token rule), the dispatcher is not wired to it (no references outside repo-call-gate.ts/its tests), and the two required test files exist and pass per the daemon's results, each case genuinely exercising what its name claims.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
1242	{"artifactId":"TASK-64703b708590bd68-s1-t3","entry":{"id":"00mvy93hg6003-ac6ca75a-388a-4bf6-848c-85c647b7e4bc","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:56:31.638Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"Both named tests exist, exercise exactly what their names claim, and the daemon reports both typecheck and tests passing. handleWorkflowApprove (src/mcp/server.ts) and withExplicitRepo (src/mcp/forward-step.ts) resolve an absolute repo and refuse before any daemon call when none can be resolved; every CLI service that calls a file-modifying table method (workflow.approvePipeline, workflow.resolveFinding, workflow.reviewArtifact, tracker.sync, tracker.setup, team.refresh/claim/release) sends an absolute repo via toAbsPath; the insrc_workflow_approve tool description was updated to reflect the absolute-repo contract. The still-present 'falls back to session workspace / INSRC_REPO' wording on insrc_present and insrc_docgen is accurate and out of scope, since their underlying RPCs (workflow.pending, docgen.generate) are read-only, not in the file-modifying table this Task gates.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
692	{"artifactId":"TASK-64703b708590bd68-s1-t4","entry":{"id":"00mvy9bulg004-6ac02952-4d3e-41b4-9c62-f8a7b416dbab","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:03:01.924Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"Both daemon tests exist, assert exactly what their names claim, and pass per the daemon's own run; typecheck passes; the code changes (gate wired into both RPCs, store written from the named repo param, no INSRC_REPO fallback) match the Task's acceptance checks, and changes stayed within the approval-family surface named by the Task.\"","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
759	{"artifactId":"TASK-64703b708590bd68-s1-t5","entry":{"id":"00mvy9royh005-118c106c-c2b5-48d2-a02c-e94747d9f594","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:15:21.113Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"fail","summary":"Typecheck and the required integration test pass, and INSRC_REPO fallbacks were correctly removed, but gating artifact.feedback.append with a mandatory `repo` param breaks every real caller of that method (its request shape never includes `repo`, only artifactPath, per legacy-request.ts and its own tests) — a genuine regression the required test doesn't exercise, so the Task is not objectively done.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
849	{"artifactId":"TASK-64703b708590bd68-s1-t5","entry":{"id":"00mvy9x06c006-82b05bbc-e135-4b53-9aba-3f2917bad1fb","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:19:28.932Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"All three acceptance checks are objectively verified against the real code and the daemon's passing typecheck/test results: every modifying-table method is now wrapped by gateHandlers() and the six named handler files no longer read process.env['INSRC_REPO'] (only a method out of scope, artifact.feedback.list, which is read-only, still does). The named integration test exists, exercises exactly what its title claims, and the daemon reports it passing with the filesystem provably unchanged.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
